<!--
    FS25_EconomyTuner default table (shipped with the mod, read on every start, replaced by mod updates).

    Do NOT edit this file to customise. Put your changes into the override files, they are layered on top of it:
        <user>/Documents/My Games/FarmingSimulator2025/modSettings/FS25_EconomyTuner/global.xml        all savegames
        <user>/Documents/My Games/FarmingSimulator2025/modSettings/FS25_EconomyTuner/savegame1.xml     one savegame slot
        <savegame folder>/FS25_EconomyTuner.xml                                                          travels with the savegame
    An override only lists the entries it changes. After editing, restart the savegame, or type  etReload
    in the developer console to apply it live (server / single player). etDump writes priceDump.csv and
    yieldDump.csv (every fillType / fruitType with name, game value and applied value).

    == <fillType name="..."> ==
    price    = sell price in EUR per 1000 L (per 1000 pieces for piece goods) as the player sees it, before
               seasonal factor and selling-point priceScale. With normalizeDifficulty the mod divides the
               difficulty multiplier out, so the value holds on EASY / NORMAL / HARD alike.
    average  = alternative to price: the year-round average (EUR per 1000 L). The base price is set to
               average / mean(factors), so the 12 seasonal prices average out to this value.
    scale    = alternative to price: multiply the price the game/map defines (e.g. scale="0.5").
    factors  = optional, 12 seasonal factors in period order 1..12 (early spring .. late winter),
               replaces the curve of the base game / map. Without it the original curve is kept.
               Seasonal price at the start of period n = price x factor n; between periods the game
               interpolates smoothly. For most crops the factors average ~1.0, so price ~ yearly average.
    buy      = price in EUR per 1000 L when the player BUYS it (seed, fertilizer, diesel at buying stations
               and the running cost of sowing / spraying / fuel). Without buy/buyScale the buy price of a
               changed fillType stays at the original game price (keepBuyPrices).
    buyScale = alternative to buy: multiply the original game price.

    == <station xmlFilename="..." fillType="..." priceScale="..."/> ==
    Selling points keep their own priceScale (e.g. HB bales x0.8, root crops x1.2 at the animal dealer).
    <station> overrides it for one selling point and fillType; xmlFilename is matched as a path suffix,
    run etDump to see the xmlFilename of every selling point.

    == <shopItem xmlFilename="..." fillType="..." markup="1" basis="best"/> ==
    Items the shop (P key) sells as consumables have a fixed price in the game. A shopItem entry makes the price
    of one unit follow the market instead: capacity (L) / 1000 x this month's price of fillType x markup.
    basis="best" (default): the highest price any selling point pays for the fillType this month (its base price
    x its priceScale x the seasonal factor of the current period, difficulty included, without random
    fluctuation, great demand or price drop). If no selling point buys the fillType the game price stays.
    basis="market": the fillType's own sell price this month, without selling point scale.
    price="N" (basis fixed, no fillType needed): a fixed price of N EUR per 1000 L, constant all year.
    Amount options (2..8 bales) scale with it. xmlFilename is matched as a path suffix.

    == <fruitType name="..."> ==
    yield        = harvest yield in litres per ha (the game stores litersPerSqm x 10000; see yieldDump.csv).
    yieldScale   = alternative to yield: multiply the game's yield (e.g. 1.2 = +20 %).
                   Straw from combines is derived from the grain ratio and does not change with yield.
    windrowScale = multiply the windrow yield (hay, silage and straw swaths) where the crop has one.
    seedScale    = multiply the seed usage per ha.

    Snapshot: base game 1.23.1 + Hof Bergmann 1.5.0.0 Beta2 (2026-09-29). Entries marked "plan 2026-10-04" follow
    FS25_非草料价格与产量调整方案.md; all other prices equal the HARD game prices.  "/t" comments = EUR per tonne.
-->
<economyTuner>
    <!--
        normalizeDifficulty  the table values are final prices: the difficulty multiplier (EASY x3 / NORMAL x1.8 on
                             sell prices) is divided out, so every difficulty shows the same prices. false = the
                             values are HARD prices and EASY / NORMAL multiply them as in the base game.
        keepBuyPrices        buying stations and running costs keep the original price of changed fillTypes.
        rescaleHistory       rescale the saved price history (economy.xml) to the new prices.
        dumpOnStart          write priceDump.csv and yieldDump.csv on every savegame start.
        checkOnStart         run the etCheck verification on every savegame start (result in log.txt and etCheck.txt).
    -->
    <settings normalizeDifficulty="true" keepBuyPrices="true" rescaleHistory="true" dumpOnStart="false"/>

